WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.840
Acquisition is the process of collecting data in a way that is authorized, documented, and appropriate for the case.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:18.180
On iPhones, common concepts include logical acquisition, backup-based acquisition, file system acquisition where lawful and technically available, and cloud or account-based acquisition.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.600
Each method has a scope, and none should be described as complete without explaining its limits.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:31.420
Logical acquisition collects accessible files, records, backups, or structured data through supported methods or forensic tools.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:41.320
Backup-based acquisition relies on backup structures that may contain many useful artifacts, including application data, media references, settings, and databases.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:52.500
Encrypted backups can be valuable because some categories of data may be unavailable or less complete in unencrypted backups, depending on method, authorization, and device conditions.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:01:01.040
File system acquisition, at a high level, may provide broader access to files and app containers when lawful authority and technical conditions support it.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:08.540
Cloud and account-based acquisition may collect iCloud data, app-specific cloud records, backups, or account artifacts.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:17.880
These methods can add evidence that is not stored locally, but they also raise scope, consent, privacy, and attribution questions that must be handled carefully.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.580
Before-first-unlock and after-first-unlock concepts help explain availability.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.720
At a high level, some protected data may not be accessible after a reboot until the device has been unlocked.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.580
Other data may remain available under different conditions.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.480
Investigators should document the state and avoid overstating what the acquisition method could or could not reach.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.060
The acquisition method affects completeness, timestamps, metadata, and defensibility.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.440
A backup may represent a point in time, not a live view of every app.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:51.420
A cloud export may reflect account state rather than local device use.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.560
A tool may parse certain artifacts while leaving others uninterpreted.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:01.700
Reports should state tools, versions, methods, scope, limitations, and assumptions clearly.
